   "text": "PORT MERROW HARBOUR TIDE GAUGE - ANNUAL DATA SUMMARY Tidewater Resilience Lab. Data processed by Samuel Achebe. Record length: 1952 to present (72 years), gaps in 1963 and 1977. Long-term trend in mean sea level: +2.9 mm per year. Trend since 1993: +4.1 mm per year. Total rise since 1952: about 21 cm. Highest recorded water levels (above mean high water springs): 1. 1.34 m - the great storm of 1987 2. 1.18 m - winter 2014 3. 1.11 m - 1953 4. 1.02 m - autumn 2020 5. 0.97 m - 1990 Number of days per year with"
  },
