   "end": 812,
   "text": "eat storm of 1987 2. 1.18 m - winter 2014 3. 1.11 m - 1953 4. 1.02 m - autumn 2020 5. 0.97 m - 1990 Number of days per year with water above the lowest section of the harbour wall: 1960s: 0.3 days per year 1990s: 1.1 days per year 2010s: 3.4 days per year Note: the rise in overtopping days is driven by both higher mean sea level and settlement of the wall. See the flood risk baseline (TRL-2024-03). Fictional sample document."
